{
  "title": "Oncogenic Osteomalacia",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/9092/oncogenic-osteomalacia",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 17 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Oncogenic Osteomalacia is a paraneoplastic syndrome of renal phosphate wasting caused by a bone or soft tissue tumor. Patients may present with osteopenia and pathologic fractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with PET/SPECT scans to identify the location of the tumor.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment involves identifying and resecting the tumor.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "age bracket",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "age of onset is late childhood to early adulthood",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the tumor secretes a **humoral factor (\"phosphatonin\")** that affects the proximal renal tubules",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "phosphatonins include FGF-23 (most important), sFRP-4, and MEPE",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "reduces calcitriol production in the kidney and inhibits phosphate transport",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "leads to increased renal phosphate excretion, hypophosphatemia and osteomalacia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "types of tumors that cause oncologic osteomalacia (known as phosphaturic mesenchymal tumor)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**benign tumors (more common)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**phosphaturic mesenchymal tumors (mixed connective tissue variant) e.g. hemangiopericytoma (commonest cause)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "osteoblastoma-like tumors",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ossifying fibrous tumors",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "nonossifying fibrous tumors",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "malignant causes (rare)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "osteosarcoma",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "fibrosarcoma",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mutations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "the key phosphatonin is FGF23, and this condition is linked to a mutation in the gene coding for FGF23",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "orthopaedic manifestations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pathological fractures of long bones and vertebrae",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "generalized bone and muscle pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "fractures of long bones, ribs and vertebrae",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "proximal muscle weakness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "fatigue",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
